.DS_Store
*.local
.zsh_history
.zcompdump*
*.backup.*

# Claude — mostly per-machine, never versioned. settings.json is 100% each
# machine's own (NOT symlinked, like ~/.gitconfig): permissions/UI config diverges
# per host and was dragging personal state into a public repo. memory/ isn't even
# symlinked anymore (see install.sh). *.backup.* is already covered above.
#
# skills/ is per-machine (`learned`, `codebase-memory`, …) and nothing versioned
# lives under claude/skills/: the `logbook` plugin is in plugins/ because it is
# shared with Antigravity. The entry guards against a skill copied in by hand.
#
# RTK.md is rtk's own command reference. `rtk init` writes it to ~/.claude/ and
# imports it from ~/.claude/CLAUDE.md — a symlink to the versioned file, so the
# import kept coming back into this public repo until binaries.sh started passing
# `--hook-only` (sep-2026). Nothing writes claude/RTK.md today; this entry is the
# guard for the day somebody copies it in to "fix" a dangling import.
claude/settings.json
claude/memory/
claude/RTK.md
claude/skills/

# Git config — per-machine (each Mac has its own credentials, 1Password vaults,
# signing keys). Only .gitignore_global is versioned.
git/.gitconfig
